## What a passkey is
A passkey lets you sign in with your fingerprint, face unlock or screen lock instead of typing a secret. Your device keeps a private key, and the website stores only a matching public key.

## Why it is safer
There is no password to steal from a website or to type into a fake page, so passkeys resist phishing.

## When passwords still matter
Not every site supports passkeys yet. Until then, use a password manager to create long, unique passwords and turn on two-factor authentication.

## What to watch
Switch on passkeys for your email and main accounts first, and keep a recovery option in case you lose your phone.
